{%- doc -%}
  Renders the cart trigger's contents: bag icon plus a "Cart (n)" label.

  SemiProbe override. Horizon renders an icon with a floating count bubble;
  the design (Figma 212:25) shows a white box containing the bag icon and the
  literal text "CART (0)". This is the smallest place to make that change —
  `cart-drawer.liquid` keeps its own trigger button and drawer behaviour, so
  the cart still opens exactly as before.

  The count is read from `cart.item_count`, so it stays live.
{%- enddoc -%}

<cart-icon
  class="
    header-actions__cart-icon sp-cart
    {% unless cart == empty %} header-actions__cart-icon--has-cart{% endunless %}
  "
  data-testid="cart-icon"
>
  <span
    class="sp-cart__icon"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
    {{ 'icon-cart.svg' | inline_asset_content }}
  </span>

  <span
    class="sp-cart__label"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
    Cart ({{ cart.item_count }})
  </span>

  {%- comment -%}
    The visible label is aria-hidden because the trigger button in
    cart-drawer.liquid already carries a full aria-label with the item count.
    A live region keeps assistive tech informed when the count changes.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <span
    class="visually-hidden"
    aria-live="polite"
  >
    {{ 'accessibility.cart_count' | t }}: {{ cart.item_count }}
  </span>
</cart-icon>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Figma 212:25 — a 95x34 white box: 2px radius, 8px inset, 4px gap, a 14x17
     bag icon and a 13/18 SemiBold uppercase label with 0.65px tracking. */
  .sp-cart {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    min-height: 34px;
    padding: 8px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
  }

  .sp-cart__icon {
    display: flex;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 14px;
    height: 17px;
  }

  /* Scoped through .header-actions__action so it outranks the theme's
     `.header-actions__action svg { width: var(--icon-size-md); height: var(
     --icon-size-md) }`, which is two classes to this rule's one and was
     winning. The width still came out at 14 because the icon span is a 14px
     flex container that squashed it, but the height stayed at the theme's
     22px and, having a definite cross size, sat flush with the span's top
     rather than centred -- putting the bag 2.63px below the cap height of
     CART beside it, which is the "not on the same line" this fixes. At 17px
     the glyph's ink centres on that cap band to within 0.13px.

     The asset's viewBox is square, so the glyph letterboxes to 14x14 inside
     the design's 14x17 box rather than stretching. That is the same ink it
     drew before; only its position changes.

     `mask` rides here too, and unconditionally. Horizon cuts a donut out of
     this svg whenever the cart is non-empty, clearing room for the count
     bubble that this design replaced with a text label:

       radial-gradient(22px at calc(100% - 2.5px) 4.5px,
                       transparent 45.45%, white 45.45%, white 100%)

     which is a 10px fully transparent core centred at (11.5, 4.5) of the
     14x17 box. The bag's top-left corner lies 9.31px from that centre and
     its bottom-right 8.90px, so the mask erases both; only the bottom-left
     corner, at 12.75px, survives -- collapsing the glyph to an "L". The
     reset this replaces was scoped `.sp-cart.header-actions__cart-icon
     --has-cart svg`, which ties Horizon's own rule at (0,2,1) and is
     declared ~25KB earlier in the compiled sheet, so order handed Horizon
     the win and the reset never took. At (0,3,1) this one outranks it
     whatever the source order.

     It is unconditional because `cart-icon.js` re-adds the --has-cart class
     on every cart update, so keying the reset to that class only invites the
     mask back. With no bubble to clear, there is never a donut to cut. */
  .header-actions__action .sp-cart .sp-cart__icon svg {
    width: 14px;
    height: 17px;
    color: #23252c;
    -webkit-mask: none;
    mask: none;
  }

  .sp-cart__label {
    color: #23252c;
    font-family: var(--font-subheading--family);
    font-weight: var(--font-subheading--weight);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 18px;
    letter-spacing: 0.65px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* The box replaces the floating bubble, so suppress the bubble. The donut
     mask that went with it is reset on the icon rule above. */
  .sp-cart .cart-bubble {
    display: none;
  }

{% endstylesheet %}
